## 3. Implementation Seam Audited

The implementation adds a narrow runtime-facing adapter:

* added `hedgehog/candidate_vector_generator.py`
* composes existing `hedgehog/local_drs_resolver.py`
* composes existing `hedgehog/candidate_vectors.py`
* composes existing `hedgehog/avf.py`
* composes existing `hedgehog/reuse_gate.py`
* composes existing `hedgehog/time_model.py`
* does not replace AVF
* does not replace candidate_vectors
* does not replace local DRS resolver
* does not create a separate store
* does not use external/global DRS
* does not use network/Gemini/LLM/embeddings

The audited path bridges the previous runtime layer into bounded scoring:

```text
Real Local DRS Resolver candidates
bounded CandidateVectors
deterministic AVF scores
ranked/reviewable candidate report
GT/LGT/Root review still required
```

## 4. Runtime Behavior Audited

Audited behavior:

* converts resolved local DRS candidates into bounded candidate vectors
* computes deterministic AVF scores
* ranks candidates for review/routing
* returns a reviewable candidate report
* preserves candidate-only semantics
* keeps GT/LGT/Root review required
* does not grant direct reuse
* does not grant action permission
* does not create FinalOutput
* does not mutate manifest
* does not mutate transition matrix
* does not call network, Gemini, connectors, external DRS, or global DRS

The generator uses deterministic signals only: domain, subject/claim keys,
controlled token overlap, freshness/TTL state, provenance refs, trace refs,
source refs, conflict flags, quarantine/deadend flags, poisoning flags, and
schema-validity as shape-only metadata.

